// field.c — a fully native (no-Python) interactive Chrono Trigger field, in C + SDL2.
// Walk Crono around a scene with the arrow keys; NPCs run their scripts live (the C VM
// scheduler), drawn as real composited sprites that animate (idle/walk); talk to NPCs to
// read dialogue in the real CT font; doors warp between scenes carrying the story flags
// forward. Foreground tiles (BG1/BG2 priority-1: counters, doorway arches, stairs, treetops)
// draw OVER the sprites, so the player walks behind them. The camera follows; collision is
// the verified sub-tile + z-plane rule.
// Everything reads ct_assets.dat — no ROM, no Python. This is play.py ported to native C.
//
//   Arrow keys : walk    X (hold) : run -- pad B, the Dash row ($00F8 bit 1)    Space / Z / Enter : talk / advance (A)
//   C : menu (the SNES X button; B = X key / Backspace closes it)    Esc : quit
// Usage: Belthasar[.exe] --assets ct_assets.dat [--scene N] [--loadflags <f>]
//        [--selftest [out.raw]] [--talk <obj>] [--gotoexit]
//   --boot            THE GAME'S OWN COLD ENTRY (disasm/notes/boot_loader.md): run C0/0057's
//                     SRAM scan, then let scene 0's boot script route -- title, then either
//                     the load screen (a cart that holds a save) or a new game. Enter = START.
//                     The cart's 8 KB lives in ct_sram.srm (CT_SRAM overrides, CT_SRAM_FRESH=1
//                     boots from an erased cart).
//   --loadcheck <srm> run FF/FAA3 over an SRAM image and print each slot's unpacked fields.
//   --sramcheck <srm> run the ROM's FF/FBE7 checksum over an SRAM image, per slot.
