      // elsewhere. $0283/$0285 are the player's world position mirrored into WRAM, which is what the ROM
      // does (measured: they track $0D84/$0D88 frame for frame). This runs AFTER the mover above, so the
      // position is this frame's. $027C = 0 is what C2/2C20 writes at the world load -- the world's init
      // script later pokes it to 1 via op $13 (C2/12C8), and the port bakes $1B9B instead of running that
      // script, but BOTH values are inside the handler's {0,1,7} gate, so it is open either way.
