        // the scripts', 1141 24B6). MEASURED (the rule's cartridge, saves/ow_w0.state, right / up / down): $0D98 (+28)
        // 03, 00, 01 while $0104 stays 01. It is the ARRIVAL byte C2/3533 reads into +28 at the lead's init -- and the
        // host wrote its own wd.pfac (1 until that init) over it every frame, so leaving the Porre ticket office ($0104 =
        // 03) Crono stood facing down (the user, 2026-10-07). A save on the map keeps the arrival byte, as the ROM does.
        // $027C IS THE OVERWORLD MODULE STATE, and the menu's entry gate reads it (C2/356A CMP #01).
        // C2/2C20 writes 0 at the world load and the world-init script pokes 1 through op $13
        // (C2/12C8); the port bakes $1B9B instead of running that script, so it writes the settled
        // value here: 1 = interactive free roam, 0 = cutscene (the new-game pan / a scripted ride,
